 br_hre_civil_war.1.title: "The imperial Civil War"
 br_hre_civil_war.1.desc: "The majority of the princes have rejected the Emperor's demand to relinquish their privileges in favour of the Empire. Now, all the prince-electors have united under the Princes' League.
The Diet has issued a warning. Within two years, the opposing factions must come together to reach an agreement. If they fail to do so, and given the temperament of both factions, war will inevitably break out between the Imperialists and the princes."

br_hre_civil_war.1.a: "May God come to Rome's aid."


 br_hre_civil_war.2.title: "The princes are on their knees!"
 br_hre_civil_war.2.desc: "VICTORY! The Emperor has defeated the vile princes who dared defy his authority. God and arms have spoken, and they have no choice but to relinquish their privileges. Far too much blood has been spilled, but it was necessary. The Western Empire has been restored!
LONG LIVE ROME! LONG LIVE THE EMPEROR!"
 br_hre_civil_war.2.a: "Oderint, dum metuant"



